From bc96483874651dad251cb703d22608071a6045c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stefanoconiglio <33290924+stefanoconiglio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:29:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Under TeXpresso, a TeX job the document stopped exits
 without a core dump

_tt_abort ends a TeX job that the document stopped: an emergency stop (an
argument left open to the end of the file, a missing \end{document}), TeX's
capacity exceeded, a hundred errors. It ended the engine with abort(), so
each of these dumped core and was reported by the system as a crash
(systemd-coredump, desktop crash notifications). Under TeXpresso they happen
all the time while text is typed: deleting the closing brace of
\input{child} together with the blank line after it is enough. The driver
copes with them already: it keeps the pages typeset so far and runs TeX
again after the next change.

So under TeXpresso, _tt_abort now ends the process with _exit(EXIT_FAILURE).
_exit rather than exit: a forked snapshot must not flush stdio buffers it
shares with the process it was forked from. Without TeXpresso, and for the
engine's own internal failures (do_abort, do_abortf), nothing changes.
---
 src/engine/main/main.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/engine/main/main.c b/src/engine/main/main.c
index 333408e..66c038b 100644
--- a/src/engine/main/main.c
+++ b/src/engine/main/main.c
@@ -62,6 +62,16 @@ NORETURN PRINTF_FUNC(1, 2) int _tt_abort(const char *format, ...)
   vfprintf(stderr, format, ap);
   va_end(ap);
   fprintf(stderr, "\n");
+  // _tt_abort ends a TeX job that the document stopped: an emergency stop
+  // (an argument left open to the end of the file, a missing \end), TeX's
+  // capacity exceeded, a hundred errors. Under TeXpresso that happens all the
+  // time while text is typed, and the driver copes: it keeps the pages typeset
+  // so far and runs TeX again after the next change. So exit without a core
+  // dump: abort() made each of them look like a crash to the system. _exit,
+  // not exit: a forked snapshot must not flush stdio buffers it shares with
+  // the process it was forked from.
+  if (texpresso)
+    _exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
   do_abort();
 }
 
